BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Purelink (NYC) w/ Umki and Discobasis
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260531T180000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260531T220000
DTSTAMP:20260525T135528
UID:ganggang-10002044-1780250400-1780264800@ganggangcafe.com.au
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/wp-content/uploads/20
 26/04/Screenshot-2026-04-28-at-3.20.07-pm.png
CREATED:20260428T052052Z
DESCRIPTION:urelink is an ambient music trio from Brooklyn\, New York City
 . The group\, comprised of Ben Paulson\, Tommy Paslaski\, and Akeem Asani\
 , formed in 2020 and has been described as an “ambient boyband.” Their
  debut release\, the single Bliss / Swivel\, was self-released in 2021\, 
 with both tracks later included on the 2023 EP To / Deep. More recently i
 n 2025 their album Faith was released\, featuring Loraine James and others
 . \n\n\n\nThe trio began collaborating after Ben Paulson\, known professio
 nally as Kindtree\, and Tommy Paslaski\, known professionally as Concave R
 eflection\, who had previously collaborated under the name All Light Hits 
 U\, met Akeem Asani\, who had been releasing under the name Millia\, in 20
 19. They began playing music together in early 2020\, using Ableton Live t
 o link their three computers over Wi-Fi\, which inspired the name Purelink
 . \n\n\n\nTo have them as part of their Australian tour is a real honour f
 or us\, we’ve been very big fans of Purelink since their first release. 
 To say the least we highly recommend coming\, sitting listening\, and gett
 ing to hear some very special music that is hard to come by. \n\n\n\nSuppo
 rts from amazing Umki and Discobasis.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260428T052054Z
LOCATION:Gang Gang Cafe\, Shop 4/2 Frencham Pl\, Downer ACT 2602
ORGANIZER:Gang Gang Cafe
URL:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/event/purelink-nyc-w-umki-and-discobasis/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mr Disco Kid (JPN)
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260607T160000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260607T220000
DTSTAMP:20260525T135528
UID:ganggang-10002049-1780848000-1780869600@ganggangcafe.com.au
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/wp-content/uploads/20
 26/05/Screenshot-2026-05-12-at-9.56.29-am.png
CREATED:20260511T235912Z
DESCRIPTION:Stoked that our friend Ross hit us up for this one. Mr Disco K
 id will be such a fun vibe for a Sunday of a long weekend…bring back the
  Sunday sesh \n\n\n\nMr Disco Kid \n\n\n\nNever Mind the Balearics are ove
 r the moon to present Japan’s hottest vinyl DJ\, “record dealer to the
  stars” and all-round champion crate digger Mr Disco Kid (aka Kouki Shin
 ada) for a long-awaited Australian debut\, this June long weekend. As a DJ
 \, his ability to surprise and delight as he jumps between genres is secon
 d to none. Combined with his emotional stage presence and infectious passi
 on for music\, he’s won the hearts of discerning dancers  \n\n\n\nworld
 wide\, getting re-booked consistently at heavyweight clubs such as London
 ’s Giant Steps\, where he’s played 7 hour sets in 2024\, 2025 and is b
 ooked again for 2026. A master discoverer and private dealer of rare recor
 ds\, his archaeological digs through vinyl history have fueled some of the
  industry’s most revered tastemakers including Luke Una\, Floating Point
 s\, Antal and The Mighty Zaff.  \n\n\n\nThe day before his visit to Austr
 alia in March 2026\, who else did Gilles Peterson (who Kouki-san calls his
  Sensei) head to for a holy grail record-buying mission in Tokyo?  \n\n\n
 \nMr Disco Kid’s long-format DJ sets build sophisticated bridges between
  complex layers of soul-jazz\, undiscovered global rhythms\, and the high-
 energy worlds of disco\, garage\, house and techno. As a trained pianist\,
  his musician’s ear guides his flow across genres\, pitches and tempos.
   \n\n\n\nHis Tokyo residency is at Shinjuku’s legendary audiophile clu
 b DJ Bar Bridge. He’s toured Europe twice so far\, guesting at clubs in 
 Germany\, France\, Ireland\, Spain and The UK. A sold-out show at Cosybox 
 New Delhi kicked off 2026 as his biggest and most adventurous year of trav
 el yet\, and he’s booked for Gilles Peterson’s We Out Here Festival 20
 26. Before hitting mainland Europe\, he’s playing another marathon at Gi
 ant Steps\, plus a night at what is arguably London’s hottest club\, Om 
 in August 
LAST-MODIFIED:20260511T235915Z
LOCATION:Gang Gang Cafe\, Shop 4/2 Frencham Pl\, Downer ACT 2602
ORGANIZER:Gang Gang Cafe
URL:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/event/mr-disco-kid-jpn/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:New York (USA) live at Gang Gang w/ Alias Error and Genie
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260613T190000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260613T230000
DTSTAMP:20260525T135528
UID:ganggang-10002054-1781377200-1781391600@ganggangcafe.com.au
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/wp-content/uploads/20
 26/05/Screenshot-2026-05-21-at-4.23.58-pm.png
CREATED:20260521T062428Z
DESCRIPTION:We are over the moon to be hosting NEW YORK on June 13th. \n\n
 \n\nTo have the incredible duo perform at Gang Gang is something we never 
 imagined. NEW YORK is a girl-pop music and performance project by artists
  Gretchen Lawrence and Coumba Samba. The sampling of royalty free loops an
 d sounds of clicks and cuts are met with chopped vocals and impulsive lyri
 cs. NEW YORK chews up the sounds and visuals of hip hop\, pop\, and electr
 o and spits them out on to the city streets. They self-released their debu
 t album No Sleep Till N.Y. in 2022. \n\n\n\nIf you are unfamiliar with the
 ir music we highly recommend you have a listen\, and grab a ticket while y
 ou’re at it. \n\n\n\nAlso\, to have Alias Error on support makes all the
  more reason to come. Alias Error is the artist moniker of Berlin/ Sydney
 -based Australian singer\, songwriter\, and DJ Alia Sèror-O’Neill. She 
 is best known for her work electronic/trip-hop duo a.s.o. alongside produc
 er Tornado Wallace\, which released its acclaimed self-titled debut album 
 in 2023. Since then\, Alias has worked with James K\, RIP Swirl\, Now Alwa
 ys Fades\, and has new works coming soon. Another incredible artist we are
  over the moon to have. \n\n\n\nDon’t forget\, we also have one of Canbe
 rra’s absolute best artists as well\, Genie playing their live set as se
 cond support. \n\n\n\nGrab a ticket before you can’t.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260521T062429Z
LOCATION:Gang Gang Cafe\, Shop 4/2 Frencham Pl\, Downer ACT 2602
ORGANIZER:Gang Gang Cafe
URL:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/event/new-york-usa-live-at-gang-gang-w-ali
 as-error-and-genie/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Hana Stretton
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260621T180000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260621T220000
DTSTAMP:20260525T135528
UID:ganggang-10001258-1782064800-1782079200@ganggangcafe.com.au
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/wp-content/uploads/20
 26/04/Screenshot-2026-04-14-at-9.43.02-am.png
CREATED:20260414T065308Z
DESCRIPTION:We are stoked to be working with Jet Black Cat again to presen
 t Hannah Stretton with Alice Barlow. \n\n\n\nHana Stretton is an accompli
 shed Australian-British multi-instrumentalist\, songwriter & producer. Bor
 n and raised on a farm in New South Wales\, Hana’s early life was steepe
 d in natural beauty and isolation\, which has become the influence for muc
 h of her music. Her work reflects a deep connection to her roots. \n\n\n\n
 Hana made her debut record\, Soon\, outside\, in still moments after fire
 s and wild storms had raged through her home in the Australian bush. Compl
 etely isolated with just her beloved cows and a few instruments\, recordin
 g music became a way to pass the hours. The album was self-released in Jan
 uary 2023\, with a vinyl run by boutique Australian label brierfield flood
  press. The following year\, P.W. Elverum & Sun (the private press of Phil
  Elvrum aka Mount Eerie) re-issued a special edition vinyl\, selling out a
 lmost instantly. Upon release\, Elvrum explained his admiration for Hana
 ’s music: “I hear an artist who has entered completely into the stream
  where creation originates […] Hana Stretton has truly recorded the deep
  flourishing sound of a quiet listening mind in full blossom.” \n\n\n\nA
 lice Barlow is a singer-songwriter\, composer and producer from South Eas
 t London known for her captivating live performances. Drawing on folk\, in
 die and alternative influences – her dark guitar tones\, haunting vocals
  and unique ear for melody have built a loyal following in London and beyo
 nd. With new singles on the way\, she is set to release her eagerly awaite
 d debut album on Domino Records this winter. This will be her first time i
 n Australia. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nGang Gang is committed to an inclusive and sa
 fe experience for all. Gang Gang Cafe is wheelchair accessible with access
 ible restrooms. We have zero tolerance for harassment and have support mea
 sures in place to ensure everyone’s safety. For specific accessibility n
 eeds or assistance\, please contact us in advance. We aim to make our even
 ts enjoyable for everyone. \n\n\n\nGang Gang Cafe acknowledges the Ngunnaw
 al and Ngambri people\, the Traditional Custodians of the land where our e
 vents take place. We pay our respects to their Elders past\, present\, and
  emerging\, and recognise their enduring connection to this land\, waters\
 , and culture. We are grateful to celebrate music and dance on Ngunnawal C
 ountry.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260414T065309Z
LOCATION:Gang Gang Cafe\, Shop 4/2 Frencham Pl\, Downer ACT 2602
ORGANIZER:Gang Gang Cafe
URL:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/event/hana-stretton/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cut Worms (USA) with special guest John Andrews (USA)
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260709T190000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260709T220000
DTSTAMP:20260525T135528
UID:ganggang-10001243-1783623600-1783634400@ganggangcafe.com.au
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/wp-content/uploads/20
 26/03/Screenshot-2026-03-17-at-11.30.21-am.png
CREATED:20260317T003144Z
DESCRIPTION:Transmitter is Max Clarke’s fourth full length record as C
 ut Worms\, due out March 13th via JagJaguwar. Produced by Jeff Tweedy at W
 ilco’s Loft studio\, Transmitter marks a deepening of Clarke’s abili
 ties and the convergence of two artists whose work searches for grace amid
  dislocation. Together\, they conjure the ecstatic spirits of power pop an
 d alt rock\, expanding Cut Worms’ vintage palette while reaffirming his 
 gift for timeless songwriting. \n\n\n\nWhile Clarke’s voice and writing 
 formed the framework\, Tweedy’s guitar and bass lines sketched the rooms
  the songs inhabit. Tweedy’s presence as a producer revealed itself not 
 in heavy-handed choices but in how he coloured spaces and continually offe
 red new textures. Between them\, their like-minded sensibilities bridged a
  generational gap to create something more nuanced than either might have 
 made alone. \n\n\n\nNow several albums into his career\, Clarke stands ful
 ly in command of his craft\, resonating at his own frequency. What began a
 s a passion for bygone pop has matured into a study of endurance itself\, 
 confirming him as a singer-songwriter of lasting depth. Transmitter finds 
 Clarke in full stride\, writing with the conviction of someone who’s mad
 e peace with uncertainty. These songs reckon with the cost of comfort and 
 return to the idea that beauty\, connection\, and love are not luxuries bu
 t necessities for survival. \n\n\n\nJohn Andrews has spent the past few ye
 ars tucked away in Red Hook\, Brooklyn – a neighborhood that sits just b
 eyond the natural drift of the city. Once shaped by maritime industry and 
 later a haven for artists in search of vast warehouse space\, its history 
 and isolation give it a quiet magnetism. Streetsweeper\, the fifth album
  by John Andrews & The Yawns\, reflects that vantage point-tranquil\, self
 -contained\, and curious about the movements most people overlook. \n\n\n\
 n\n\n\n\nGang Gang is committed to an inclusive and safe experience for al
 l. Gang Gang Cafe is wheelchair accessible with accessible restrooms. We h
 ave zero tolerance for harassment and have support measures in place to en
 sure everyone’s safety. For specific accessibility needs or assistance\,
  please contact us in advance. We aim to make our events enjoyable for eve
 ryone. \n\n\n\nGang Gang Cafe acknowledges the Ngunnawal and Ngambri peopl
 e\, the Traditional Custodians of the land where our events take place. We
  pay our respects to their Elders past\, present\, and emerging\, and reco
 gnise their enduring connection to this land\, waters\, and culture. We ar
 e grateful to celebrate music and dance on Ngunnawal Country.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260414T065350Z
LOCATION:Gang Gang Cafe\, Shop 4/2 Frencham Pl\, Downer ACT 2602
ORGANIZER:Gang Gang Cafe
URL:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/event/cut-worms-usa-with-special-guest-joh
 n-andrews-usa/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Leah Senior
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260809T180000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260809T220000
DTSTAMP:20260525T135528
UID:ganggang-10002052-1786298400-1786312800@ganggangcafe.com.au
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/wp-content/uploads/20
 26/05/Screenshot-2026-05-19-at-10.19.38-am.png
CREATED:20260519T002012Z
DESCRIPTION:Australian folk diviner Leah Senior makes her way to Canberr
 a with her band in June to launch her fifth studio album Pt. Roadknight.P
 t. Roadknight explores Leah’s introspective\, nature-loving side while 
 honing the singular baroque psych folk that has captivated listeners aroun
 d the world. While the style and instrumentation of ‘70s Brit folk are t
 ouchstones on Senior’s forthcoming album\, her disarming lyrics are fres
 h and wholehearted\, wrestling with modern concerns of gentrification and 
 isolation while finding solace in the quiet beauty of the Victoria surf co
 ast town where she lives. \n\n\n\nA shining star of the Australian folk sc
 ene for the past decade\, Leah Senior’s past four records have received 
 critical acclaim from global media and radio stations\, with Leah touring 
 extensively\, sharing stages with the likes of Wilco\, Iron & Wine\, Simon
  Joyner\, Jessica Pratt\, and King Gizzard and The Lizard Wizard.  \n\n\n
 \nThe new album Pt. Roadknight marks an exciting new chapter in Leah Sen
 ior’s musical journey\, affirming her as one of Australia’s most authe
 ntic folk storytellers.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260519T002015Z
LOCATION:Gang Gang Cafe\, Shop 4/2 Frencham Pl\, Downer ACT 2602
ORGANIZER:Gang Gang Cafe
URL:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/event/leah-senior/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Select Music presents Felipe Baldomir 'Sunset Highway' Tour
DTSTART;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260827T190000
DTEND;TZID=Australia/Sydney:20260827T223000
DTSTAMP:20260525T135528
UID:ganggang-10002050-1787857200-1787869800@ganggangcafe.com.au
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/wp-content/uploads/20
 26/05/Screenshot-2026-05-12-at-10.00.06-am.png
CREATED:20260512T000241Z
DESCRIPTION:Words from Felipe: \n\n\n\n“Australia! I am so excited to be
  heading on tour this winter (Jul-Sep) to celebrate the first four singles
  of my upcoming fourth album! \n\n\n\nThe new music is already starting to
  drop\, and I cannot wait to play it live alongside the classic favourites
 ! The Sunset Highway Australian Tour 2026 is now on sale – let’s go!!
 ” \n\n\n\nFelipe Baldomir is a coastal indie-folk singer-songwriter and 
 multi-instrumentalist from Uruguay\, now based in Byron Bay\, Australia. \
 n\n\n\nKnown for his feel-good sound & dynamic live-looping performances\,
  he blends folk with groovy guitar riffs\, drums\, synths\, and saxophone 
 to deliver a full-band energy show as a solo artist. Since relocating to A
 ustralia in 2018\, Felipe has built a global audience through relentless t
 ouring – evolving from busking and van life into sold-out headline shows
  and festival appearances across Europe\, the UK\, Australia\, North Ameri
 ca\, and beyond. \n\n\n\nFelipe has just announced that his fourth studio 
 album will arrive this November 2026.Featuring a wave of fresh coastal sou
 nds inspired by outdoor living in Australia and a deep connection to surfi
 ng\, his songwriting reflects a sense of flow\, openness\, and adventure. 
 Felipe writes with the stage in mind\, making the music all about bringing
  people together &creating an uplifting experience. With a strong internat
 ional touring presence and a reputation for engaging live shows\, Felipe i
 s steadily carving out his place within the global indie scene. \n\n\n\nTh
 e Sunset Highway Australian Tour 2026 is now live & on sale.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260512T000244Z
LOCATION:Gang Gang Cafe\, Shop 4/2 Frencham Pl\, Downer ACT 2602
ORGANIZER:Gang Gang Cafe
URL:https://ganggangcafe.com.au/event/select-music-presents-felipe-baldomi
 r-sunset-highway-tour/
END:VEVENT
